--
N5008 [dcl.init.general]/16.6.2.2 (C++20, P0960): `point a(4)' initializes
the aggregate's first element from 4.  With several expressions, or for
an aggregate that is not a POD, this worked; a POD aggregate with one
expression that does not convert to it was assigned from it ("invalid
implicit conversion from 'signed int' to 'struct point'", bin53).  Before
C++20 the program is ill-formed, which the front end still reports.
g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG
assertion.
